"""Single-use application of scan011 visual adjudications."""
from pathlib import Path
import csv,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];ch={}
first={x['box']:x['reading'] for x in csv.DictReader((R/'second/149_scan011_first.tsv').open(),delimiter='\t')}
def c(k,e,final=None):
 ch[k]={'personally_inspected':True,'selection':'first' if final is None else 'custom','evidence':e,'changed':'no' if final is None else 'yes'}
 if final is not None:ch[k]['final']=final
c('b01','The dark numeral has a horizontal cap and rounded lower body: 5. The second answer omitted only the author-page wrapper.')
c('b03','The live p has a descender while its following t starts above the p body and ends at its top level: the t is raised, not baseline. Correct that position. The cancelled last cluster has a low bowl and tall final stroke, with the strike obscuring the first descender and junction; pt, dt and ch cannot be separated securely. Keep the cancellation, broaden that local doubt, and retain the independent insertion before the cancelled phrase. The long initial curve is its leader, not a parenthesis.',first['b03'].replace('est le pt générique','est le p$^t$ générique').replace(r'\unsure{pt}',r'\unsure{pt|dt|ch}'))
c('b04','The abbreviation has a visibly raised t, and conn has a separate terminal stop. Math superscript and textsuperscript represent the same raised letter; retain the first macro convention.')
c('b05','Two short bars form the relation; the upper bends and the lower is irregular, so the similarity/equality ambiguity remains. No heads support a double arrow. Keep similarity first from the wavy upper component. The cancelled K with low zero and separate live k, both abbreviation stops and enclosing parentheses are visible. Deleted math wrappers and mathbb braces are syntax.')
c('b07','After c, o and the two n arches, the u leads into a single long terminal return ending in the s curve. No independently formed e body occurs between u and that curve. Keep connus; grammatical agreement is not used to add e.')
c('b08','The small two-leg pi begins below the E capital roof and matches the kernel notation of scans009–010; retain lowercase pi. In the cancelled symbol the two legs survive but its roof/junction is crossed, so its existing pi doubt remains. The tilde above the right arrow, lower leftward limit arrow, dotted i index, full barred-K/K index and both eta arguments are present. Dollars, bar spelling and braces are syntax.')
c('b09','The pi is small beside the full-height Gamma and U, supporting the same lowercase convention. The inner argument parenthesis is complete. Both upper and lower returns of the larger outer enclosing close survive at the paper edge, establishing its existence despite the missing extreme right. Keep the outer parenthesis and the marginal status; the black image edge is not an added stroke.')
c('b10','Both U indices, overbars, tensor cross and k index, double-stroked rational Q and formula number 11 agree. The differences are display wrappers and bar/overline syntax.')
c('b12','Every two-leg kernel/fundamental-group sign is small beside U and the lower capital Gamma, and matches the pi forms in b08,b09,b14,b16; keep pi throughout. The underbrace begins under the full first term and its lower label includes two equality strokes. Vertical pairs remain equalities; all horizontal heads and both terminal 1s are visible. The final Gamma has a live raised hook/prime and a separately cancelled subscript. Its rounded first body favors barred Q, but the heavy diagonal cancellations also admit barred k; retain that additional alternative. Empty cells, spacing, wrappers and placement of the prime in TeX are representation only.',first['b12'].replace(r'\unsure{\overline{\mathbb Q}/k}',r'\unsure{\overline{\mathbb Q}/k|\bar k/k}'))
c('b13','The source diagram is marginal. Every object, bar, equality, index and connector agrees: only Spec(K) to U_i has a definite downward V head; the other dark ends remain shafts. The two small isolated dark points below the top-right object have no relation label, aligned punctuation position or attached text. Do not promote them to an arbitrary colon in an empty diagram cell. Bar/overline, mathbb braces, spacing and wrapper differences are syntax.')
c('b14','Both pi signs are at the small level relative to U and the argument parentheses, with the same straight-legged form seen in b08 and b12. Keep lowercase pi. The two equality bars, all indices and overbars agree; dollars and bar spelling are syntax.')
c('b15','A thin 1 with slanted entry precedes a closed oval zero: 10. This is lower-left foliation in the thin hand, not the bold author-page number; retain margin.')
c('b16','The initial pi is the same small two-leg form. The E has a heavily retraced upright and three arms; the pale extra upright follows the same stem and does not provide a separable cancelled letter or distinct strike. Keep ordinary E without inventing an illegible predecessor. Both i indices, eta bar, equality and comma are present.')
(R/'documentation/149_scan011_audit_choices.json').write_text(json.dumps(ch,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
p=R/'pages/149_scan011.tex';s=p.read_text().replace('est le pt générique','est le p$^t$ générique').replace(r'\unsure{pt}',r'\unsure{pt|dt|ch}').replace(r'\unsure{\overline{\mathbb Q}/k}',r'\unsure{\overline{\mathbb Q}/k|\bar k/k}');p.write_text(s)
p=R/'reviews/149_scan011.json';r=json.loads(p.read_text());cs={x['id']:x for x in r['changes']}
def box(b):
 q=next(q for q in r['audit_boxes'] if q['box']==b);return [q[k] for k in ('x0','y0','x1','y1')]
for i,b in [('c04','b03'),('c05','b03'),('c16','b12')]:
 x=cs[i];x['final']=x['final'].replace(r'\unsure{pt}',r'\unsure{pt|dt|ch}').replace(r'\unsure{\overline{\mathbb Q}/k}',r'\unsure{\overline{\mathbb Q}/k|\bar k/k}')
 x.update(evidence=ch[b]['evidence'],crop=f'crops/149_scan011_second_{b}.png',box=box(b))
r['changes'].append({'id':'audit_b03_raised_t','place':'Notons insertion, abbreviation before générique','C':'pt','H':'pt','final':'p$^t$','evidence':ch['b03']['evidence'],'crop':'crops/149_scan011_second_b03.png','box':box('b03'),'confidence':'high','against_C':True,'against_H':True,'kind':'misread symbol or index','error_category':'Symbols and indices','marked_in_H':False,'mathematical':False})
for d in r['doubts']:
 if d['place']=='cancelled phrase after courbes.':d.update(reading=r'\deleted{Ceci dit, le \unsure{pt|dt|ch}}',alternatives=['pt','dt','ch'],reason=ch['b03']['evidence'])
 if d['place']=='display (12), crossed subscript after Gamma-prime':d.update(reading=r'\deleted{\unsure{\overline{\mathbb Q}/k|\bar k/k}}',alternatives=[r'\overline{\mathbb Q}/k',r'\bar k/k'],reason=ch['b12']['evidence'])
r['notes'].append('Independent audit: all13 differing boxes were inspected. The t in the inserted p raised t générique is raised and has been corrected. The cancelled final cluster now records pt|dt|ch, and the cancelled Gamma-prime subscript records barred Q/k|barred k/k. Small angular pi is retained across all six mathematical crops by its level/size relative to E, Gamma and U. The marginal diagram’s two detached points remain unassigned marks, not a supplied colon; the heavy inline E has no recoverable separate predecessor.')
r['hand'].append({'habit':'A tall t immediately after a short p can be a raised abbreviation letter.','pages':[11],'consistency':'In the Notons insertion its foot is at the p body’s upper level; the following prose pt is not changed merely by analogy.','misread':'Both witnesses flattened the inserted p raised t to pt.'})
p.write_text(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
